WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.950 --> 00:00:03.587
What if it never rained again?

2
00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:12.111
Rain is how fresh water comes back to land. Without it, ponds and rivers would slowly shrink.

3
00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:19.386
Even the Atacama, the driest desert, gets a little rain. Parts of it have gone years without any.

4
00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:27.433
Wells and desalination could buy some time. But about eighty percent of the world’s cropland is watered only by rain.

5
00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:31.950
And here’s the strange part. The oceans would keep evaporating.

6
00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:38.946
With no rain to bring it down, the water vapor would have nowhere to go. The air would just get more and more humid.

7
00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:43.567
Every raindrop is water coming home.
